[Study "Black Plays 3...Nd4 and 3...f5"]
[Video "/downloader/downloads/Italian Center Attack/03-02 Move 3 Sidelines - Black Plays 3...Nd4 and 3...f5.mp4"]
[Orientation "white"]

{In this study, I want to show you two gambits that Black could try to play! We have to learn them to avoid their traps.}
1. e4 e5 {Once again, 1.e4 e5.} 2. Nf3 Nc6 {Both knights are developed to their natural squares. We play Bc4 here and enter the Italian.} 3. Bc4 Nd4 {This is the Blackburne Gambit. If we take on e5, ...Qg5 is good for Black (a famous trap). So instead, we simply trade knights and double Black's pawns. [%cal Gf3e5] [%csl Rd4]} (3... f5 {This is the Rousseau Gambit. If we accept the pawn, Black gets full compensation and good attacking chances with ...e4. Instead, we'll push with d4. [%cal Ge4f5,Re5e4]} 4. d4 fxe4 {Black can take on e4. This is the most popular move. We can counter by grabbing the pawn on e5, opening up our queen in the process. [%csl Re5]} (4... exd4 {Black can also choose to take on d4. We should recapture with the knight, which also opens up our queen.} 5. Nxd4 Nf6 {5...Nf6 covers our queen's checking square. We'll play 6.Nc3 to support our e4-pawn. [%csl Rh5]} 6. Nc3 fxe4 {Black takes on e4.} 7. Bg5 {We have maximum pressure on e4 and by extension on Black's entire position. We're going to castle. f3 to open up our rook is also a powerful idea to increase pressure on the knight. [%cal Ge1g1,Gf2f3] [%csl Re4,Rf6]}) 5. Nxe5 Nxe5 {Black trades knights. This is already a huge mistake.} (5... d5 {5...d5 is one of the best moves under the circumstances for Black. We can simply pin the knight.} 6. Bb5 Qd6 {Black defends the knight using their queen. [%csl Rc6]} 7. c4 {We simply are too ahead in development and activity. 7...dxc4 8.Nc3 attacks e4. We will simply be getting turbo development and Black is in trouble. They won't be able to defend everything. [%cal Gb1c3,Ge1g1]}) 6. dxe5 {It's very hard to stop Qd5. The engine gives us a +2 advantage. [%cal Rd1d5] [%csl Rd5]}) 4. Nxd4 exd4 {Black recaptures.} 5. O-O {And we castle. We'll be calm about this, and play slow, improving moves like c3 and Re1. [%cal Gf1e1,Gc2c3]} *
